1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,218
IoT Scanner gives you a local view of nearby Bluetooth low
energy advertisers and Wi-Fi networks.

2
00:00:06,218 --> 00:00:08,400
This walkthrough uses simulated demo devices.

3
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:15,806
Choose Nearby, Balanced, Wide, or a custom signal threshold.

4
00:00:15,806 --> 00:00:17,624
Your device list updates immediately.

5
00:00:17,624 --> 00:00:21,261
Signal strength is a filter, not a distance in meters.

6
00:00:22,933 --> 00:00:25,479
Review new high and medium priority signals.

7
00:00:25,479 --> 00:00:29,115
Each match includes the signal level and its detection category.

8
00:00:29,115 --> 00:00:30,933
Unverified signatures remain clearly labeled.

9
00:00:32,133 --> 00:00:35,770
Record the devices already in your surroundings as a baseline.

10
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:39,042
Baseline devices stay visible without producing new device
alerts.

11
00:00:40,267 --> 00:00:43,176
Select a device and open Find this device.

12
00:00:43,176 --> 00:00:46,812
Move a few steps, then pause and compare fresh readings.

13
00:00:46,812 --> 00:00:51,903
The app shows whether the signal is getting stronger, holding
steady, or getting weaker.

14
00:00:51,903 --> 00:00:55,539
It also displays recent history and the last reception time.

15
00:00:55,539 --> 00:00:59,176
Signal strength does not provide an exact direction or distance.

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,727
Export observations as a CSV report when you want to keep a
record.

17
00:01:13,727 --> 00:01:16,273
No account or cloud connection is required.

18
00:01:16,273 --> 00:01:21,000
Scan data stays on your phone until you choose where to save it.
